# Generated plan-auditor state. Everything under this directory is machine
# output: evidence chains, seals, the agent registry, monitor checkpoints and
# daemon state. Ignoring it by default means a new runtime file is protected
# from an accidental commit the moment the tool writes it, instead of only
# after somebody notices it and adds a line to the repository .gitignore.
#
# Hand-authored input is re-included below. ``plan.json`` (and any named plan
# under ``plans/``) is what you write; ``request-source.json`` is the host
# request the workspace was activated from; ``.gitignore`` is this file.
*
!.gitignore
!plan.json
!request-source.json
!plans/
!/plans/**
